From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: dynamic properties (style setExpression, getExpression, removeExpression; recalc)

IHTMLStyle2::setExpression evaluates the expression in the page's script engine (the named language, else JScript) and sets the property to its value as a script assignment would; document.recalc evaluates every element's expressions again; getExpression gives the expression text, removeExpression drops it (VARIANT_TRUE when there was one). They were E_NOTIMPL. Expressions in style sheets (expression() values) are not read; there is no automatic re-evaluation, only recalc.
